WEBVTT

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:03.890
We've reached the semifinal 
round of the tournament finals!

00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:05.890
This is the second match of the second fight!

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:08.830
The match is approaching its middle stage!

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:13.200
It's Yuri Usui from Team Caesar...

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.190
...versus Misaki Tokura from Team Q4!

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:20.260
<i>Oh</i>! Yuri has quite the lineup!

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:23.830
In particular, the Dailadies on the left 
and right is a point worth mentioning.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:29.090
Prepare yourself!

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:12.520
Cosmo Roar's skill!

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:15.780
I add +2000 to the power of Enigman Wave!

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:22.640
Enigman Wave's power is 12000...

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:30.400
If Dailady's attack hits, another 
unit can get +3000 power.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.990
Naturally, she would give the power to...

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:39.360
On top of that, at the beginning of Enigman 
Wave's attack, if its power is 14000 or above,

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:41.230
it gains a new skill.

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:45.990
That skill to draw a card 
if its attack hits...

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:49.670
In that case...

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:53.940
I attack Goddess of the Half 
Moon, Tsukuyomi with Dailady!

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:56.830
I guard with Dream Eater!

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:02.430
Next, I attack with the Dailady on my left!

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:04.010
I guard with Gemini!

00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:11.900
She sees right through her opponent's 
strategy and protects against it! That's our Misaki!

00:03:12.570 --> 00:03:16.520
Not bad. She was able to protect 
herself against Wave's power increase.

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:18.390
But... I'm not done yet.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:20.740
With a boost from Magical Police, Quilt,

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:23.110
Enigman Wave attacks!

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:26.040
Drive check!

00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:32.160
Even though Misaki protected 
herself against the powering up...

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:33.670
She got a critical?!

00:03:33.670 --> 00:03:34.930
GC, yo?!

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:37.530
I give all the effects to Enigman Wave!

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:45.570
Caesar's Empress

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:52.810
Since the attack hit, 
Quilt's skill activates!

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:54.780
I switch a card from my hand.

00:03:57.850 --> 00:03:59.480
That's the end of my turn.

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:01.930
She's lucky with drawing triggers...

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:05.130
But... I'm not going to lose!

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:06.280
I draw!

00:04:07.670 --> 00:04:11.280
With Goddess of the Half Moon's skill, I 
get to check the top five cards of my deck.

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:13.830
No triggers...

00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:17.920
Beautiful, shining goddess!

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:18.810
I ride...

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:26.500
Misaki is riding Amaterasu!

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:28.650
Show her the power of a grade 3!

00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:33.730
Amaterasu's skill! I Soulcharge, 
then check the top card of my deck.

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:36.480
I put the card to the bottom of the deck.

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:40.570
So far, I haven't come across any triggers...

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:45.740
The odds are good that a trigger will 
come up during my next drive check.

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:48.450
This Amaterasu will make it happen!

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:52.190
I attack Dailady with Battle 
Maiden, Tagitsuhime!

00:04:56.910 --> 00:05:00.850
I see. She wants to remove the 
Dailadies, who can intercept.

00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:03.540
Amaterasu attacks Enigma Wave!

00:05:03.790 --> 00:05:04.920
No guard!

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:06.920
Twin drive check!

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:12.260
There it is! I got a critical trigger!

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:20.530
That's the end of my turn.

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:24.800
Wow! To draw a trigger right there...

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:28.990
I'm sure Misaki knew the chances were high.

00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:32.540
She will have remembered the 
cards she checked earlier.

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:36.700
I get it! Misaki's memory really is awesome!

00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:39.650
She also calculates future probabilities,

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:42.690
moving closer to the sure thing 
that will bring her victory.

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:45.410
That's Misaki's way of fighting.

00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:47.710
I draw!

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:52.230
Beautiful, shining superwoman of love!

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:53.440
I ride...

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:07.840
And then...

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:08.670
...I call...

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:14.300
Next, I activate Cosmo Roar's skill again!

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:16.230
I give the power to Enigman Rain!

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:22.550
Enigman Rain, 12000...

00:06:25.290 --> 00:06:28.480
I see. That's what she's after...

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:31.120
I attack Tagitsuhime with Dailady!

00:06:32.930 --> 00:06:38.420
She intends to keep me from intercepting, 
so Enigman Rain's attack will go through...

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:40.400
...but...

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:44.620
With a boost from Daisy, Miracle 
Beauty attacks Amaterasu!

00:06:48.210 --> 00:06:50.490
With a boost from Magical Police, Quilt,

00:06:50.490 --> 00:06:53.430
Enigman Rain attacks Amaterasu!

00:06:56.090 --> 00:06:57.360
Oh, no you don't!

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:00.320
I guard with Psychic Bird 
and White Hare of Inaba!

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:04.600
Twin drive check!

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:13.390
That's the end of my turn.

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:15.910
Impressive...

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:20.820
Just what I expected. She 
minimized the damage.

00:07:20.820 --> 00:07:23.570
She protected herself against Rain's attack.

00:07:23.570 --> 00:07:27.110
Since she's got a limited 
hand, it was her best option.

00:07:27.610 --> 00:07:31.770
If Enigman Rain's power reaches 
12000 or higher and its attack hits,

00:07:31.770 --> 00:07:35.730
another unit can stand.

00:07:35.730 --> 00:07:38.350
And if she stands Miracle Beauty,

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:42.390
the card next to it...

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:46.840
She can activate that card's skill to 
make the rear-guard Daisy stand, too.

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:50.100
If even one of Rain's attacks goes through,

00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:52.820
it'll mean enduring another 
attack from the right side.

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:58.260
She managed to figure all that out. They 
didn't give her the second match for nothing.

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:00.260
Still, Misaki...

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:05.380
Team Caesar's Empress is 
going to go beyond that.

00:08:05.930 --> 00:08:08.330
You've made an accurate 
assessment of the situation.

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:10.440
But...

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:12.690
...in your shoes, I think I would've been...

00:08:12.690 --> 00:08:14.000
...a little more adventurous.

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:18.570
I'm more interested in 
certainty than adventures!

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:22.910
I activate Amaterasu's skill!

00:08:28.280 --> 00:08:30.630
This will come with a drive check!

00:08:31.620 --> 00:08:32.580
I call...

00:08:38.540 --> 00:08:40.390
White Hare of Inaba's skill!

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:42.630
One of the cards in my hand goes to the Soul.

00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:48.420
Ichibyoshi, Crescent Moon, and 
Half Moon are in the Soul!

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:53.260
This way, Goddess of the Full Moon, 
Tsukuyomi, can be used to attack with 11000 power!

00:08:53.430 --> 00:08:56.360
Show her some grade 3 girl power!

00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:58.040
Go for it, Misaki!

00:08:58.810 --> 00:09:00.930
I'm going to keep Dailady from intercepting!

00:09:01.550 --> 00:09:04.090
I attack with Goddess of 
the Full Moon, Tsukuyomi!

00:09:07.620 --> 00:09:12.020
Amaterasu attacks Enigman Rain 
with a boost from White Hare!

00:09:13.270 --> 00:09:15.800
I guard with Cosmo Fang and Justice Cobalt!

00:09:18.430 --> 00:09:20.830
That's a total of 30000 shield!

00:09:20.830 --> 00:09:24.620
Wow... She had that much 
defensive power left...

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:27.510
Twin drive, first check...

00:09:31.140 --> 00:09:33.670
16000 versus 30000...

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:35.830
Right now, Yuri has 4 damage.

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:40.020
Should I give this critical 
trigger to Amaterasu?

00:09:40.020 --> 00:09:42.550
Or to Full Moon?

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:45.800
If I give it to Amaterasu,

00:09:45.800 --> 00:09:50.370
and a draw trigger comes up 
during my second check...

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:52.890
...I'll win...

00:09:55.300 --> 00:09:59.130
But the attack won't be able to go through 
with anything other than a draw trigger.

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:02.370
The critical effects will be wasted, too...

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:06.970
In which case... I should 
give the effects to...

00:10:08.260 --> 00:10:10.330
...Goddess of the Full Moon, Tsukuyomi!

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:14.550
I give all the effects to Goddess 
of the Full Moon, Tsukuyomi!

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:17.590
+1 critical and +5000 power!

00:10:20.380 --> 00:10:21.250
Sure.

00:10:22.460 --> 00:10:24.070
That's what you would normally do.

00:10:42.150 --> 00:10:43.360
It was close, huh?

00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:49.620
If you'd given Ginger's critical to 
Amaterasu, I would have taken 2 damage.

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:52.050
This fight would be over.

00:10:52.710 --> 00:10:56.110
I know the choice you 
faced about the trigger.

00:10:56.110 --> 00:10:59.010
You want to gain any advantage 
in a fight, no matter how small.

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:02.320
So you chose the option with 
the higher chance of success.

00:11:05.100 --> 00:11:06.970
There's nothing wrong with that.

00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:08.830
But, you know...

00:11:09.470 --> 00:11:11.620
...there's no guarantee that you're 
always going to win like that!

00:11:13.220 --> 00:11:16.500
I give this draw trigger to Goddess 
of the Full Moon, Tsukuyomi!

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:17.680
And then...

00:11:17.680 --> 00:11:19.340
...I attack Enigman Rain!

00:11:20.600 --> 00:11:21.430
Guard!

00:11:25.210 --> 00:11:26.210
This, too...

00:11:29.710 --> 00:11:31.860
21000 versus 20000!

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:39.690
Next...

00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:52.060
That's the end of my turn.

00:11:52.700 --> 00:11:54.190
It's too bad.

00:11:54.910 --> 00:11:57.810
Thanks to that, I used up my whole hand, too.

00:11:59.670 --> 00:12:03.190
Okay, now I'll show you the way I fight.

00:12:03.970 --> 00:12:06.170
That is, my image of how to win.

00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:12.390
Instead of worrying about probabilities, 
I pull out all the stops.

00:12:12.700 --> 00:12:13.780
When I do that...

00:12:16.720 --> 00:12:19.820
...the cards will answer my call!

00:12:34.580 --> 00:12:35.460
I draw!

00:12:36.840 --> 00:12:38.690
I call Miracle Beauty!

00:12:41.960 --> 00:12:43.530
Cosmo Roar's skill!

00:12:43.530 --> 00:12:45.860
I add +2000 to the power of Enigman Rain!

00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:50.630
With a boost from Daisy,

00:12:50.630 --> 00:12:53.130
Miracle Beauty attacks Amaterasu!

00:12:56.050 --> 00:12:58.370
With a boost from Magical Police, Quilt,

00:12:58.370 --> 00:13:00.850
Enigman Rain attacks Amaterasu!

00:13:02.560 --> 00:13:04.120
It's the same as before.

00:13:04.120 --> 00:13:06.590
If Enigman Rain's attack goes through,

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:09.220
Miracle Beauty and Daisy will stand.

00:13:09.840 --> 00:13:10.850
I won't let it!

00:13:11.210 --> 00:13:13.490
I guard with Ginger and Dream Eater!

00:13:16.250 --> 00:13:18.600
The same kind of guard as before...

00:13:19.210 --> 00:13:20.000
Except...

00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:25.660
...even if Rain's attack doesn't go through, 
it's possible for Miracle Beauty to stand.

00:13:25.660 --> 00:13:27.970
As long as a stand trigger shows up...

00:13:27.970 --> 00:13:32.610
Then Daisy will also stand, and I 
can attack again with full power.

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:35.940
You don't draw triggers 
based on probabilities.

00:13:35.940 --> 00:13:38.350
You draw them with a strong 
will that desires victory.

00:13:38.850 --> 00:13:39.900
Twin drive...

00:13:40.370 --> 00:13:41.600
First check!

00:13:50.380 --> 00:13:51.750
Second check!

00:13:54.990 --> 00:13:55.870
It can't be...

00:14:01.680 --> 00:14:03.330
Stand trigger?

00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:06.470
Misaki!

00:14:06.990 --> 00:14:10.250
This is Yuri... Team Caesar's Empress...

00:14:10.810 --> 00:14:13.060
She summoned a trigger, as 
she would a loyal subject.

00:14:14.400 --> 00:14:15.870
Stand trigger!

00:14:16.970 --> 00:14:20.590
Miracle Beauty, stand! +5000 power.

00:14:21.070 --> 00:14:22.910
And then I activate her skill...

00:14:22.910 --> 00:14:24.680
...to make Daisy stand!

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:28.090
I'm going to send her to finish you off.

00:14:28.090 --> 00:14:32.480
With a boost from Daisy, Miracle 
Beauty attacks Amaterasu!

00:14:46.850 --> 00:14:49.470
Caesar  Yuri Usui
Q4  Misaki Tokura

00:14:47.150 --> 00:14:50.940
The winner is Yuri Usui from Team Caesar!

00:14:57.120 --> 00:15:01.280
I don't believe it... Misaki lost...

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:05.820
That one draw...

00:15:06.520 --> 00:15:09.870
It was close. You had a chance to win there.

00:15:10.610 --> 00:15:14.030
During a fight, there's a moment 
where the chance of winning arrives,

00:15:14.030 --> 00:15:16.180
and it bypasses all plans and probabilities.

00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:21.460
Finding that moment is really 
important to me, see...

00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:23.770
Yuri...

00:15:24.470 --> 00:15:27.560
Well, that's one kind of 
fighting style, anyway.

00:15:43.010 --> 00:15:44.480
That was a shame.

00:15:46.030 --> 00:15:49.330
That was my first time against 
someone who fights like that.

00:15:49.330 --> 00:15:50.630
That's right.

00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:52.800
Misaki, the way you fight...

00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:57.910
...is to seek out the highest probability, 
calculate, and think it through.

00:15:57.910 --> 00:16:00.090
Certainly, it's a different 
style than Yuri's.

00:16:00.620 --> 00:16:01.520
But...

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:04.120
...it's not a question 
of which is good or bad.

00:16:04.120 --> 00:16:06.160
Mastering your own way of fighting...

00:16:06.390 --> 00:16:08.900
...is important for a fighter.

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:11.350
That's what I believe.

00:16:14.690 --> 00:16:15.430
Yeah.

00:16:18.880 --> 00:16:23.640
At last, the third match of the second 
fight of the semifinals is about to begin!

00:16:23.640 --> 00:16:25.150
It's s-<i>o</i> exciting, isn't it?

00:16:25.150 --> 00:16:29.340
Team Caesar Kenji Mitsusada 
vs 
Team Q4 Aichi Sendou

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:28.920
It's Aichi Sendou versus Kenji Mitsusada!

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:32.680
The team that advances to the final round 
depends on the outcome of this fight.

00:16:31.080 --> 00:16:32.680
Well, here I go.

00:16:32.680 --> 00:16:36.810
Your opponent is the leader of Team Caesar, 
a really tough rival among tough rivals.

00:16:36.810 --> 00:16:38.850
But I'm sure you can do it, Brother!

00:16:39.150 --> 00:16:40.240
Thank you.

00:16:57.330 --> 00:17:00.620
The team that wins this fight 
will be pitted against us.

00:17:00.620 --> 00:17:05.230
Hmph. Whichever one wins, they'll 
be no challenge for AL4.

00:17:09.050 --> 00:17:13.840
That power subdues and humiliates everyone.

00:17:14.270 --> 00:17:19.990
Vanguard fighting isn't about subduing 
people or anything like that.

00:17:21.960 --> 00:17:26.010
I'm going to stick with a Vanguard 
fight that's different from yours.

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:32.210
Show me your "different" Vanguard fight.

00:17:34.100 --> 00:17:36.150
Here we are at last, Aichi.

00:17:36.310 --> 00:17:37.990
Kamui and Gai...

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:41.340
Then Misaki and Yuri...

00:17:41.340 --> 00:17:43.100
They were both wonderful fights.

00:17:43.670 --> 00:17:47.650
I want to share a fight like that with you!

00:17:49.810 --> 00:17:52.110
Aichi, I like your face like this.

00:17:56.890 --> 00:17:58.520
Let's have a supreme fight!

00:18:01.330 --> 00:18:02.160
Right!

00:18:07.740 --> 00:18:10.840
This is the Vanguard Championship 
Final Tournament!

00:18:11.090 --> 00:18:13.920
Let the third match of 
the semifinals... begin!

00:18:14.450 --> 00:18:16.420
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:18:21.880 --> 00:18:23.370
Wingal Brave!

00:18:23.840 --> 00:18:25.140
Enigman Flow!

00:18:25.640 --> 00:18:26.530
I draw.

00:18:27.590 --> 00:18:29.870
I ride Enigman Ripple.

00:18:34.190 --> 00:18:35.870
I activate Enigman Flow's skill...

00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:40.300
...and on top of that, 
Enigman Ripple's skill.

00:18:43.240 --> 00:18:44.480
That's the end of my turn.

00:18:44.480 --> 00:18:45.410
I draw.

00:18:46.400 --> 00:18:48.930
I ride Little Sage, Marron!

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:54.840
I move Wingal Brave...

00:18:55.470 --> 00:18:56.970
...and call Barcgal!

00:18:57.470 --> 00:18:59.950
I also superior call Flogal!

00:19:02.310 --> 00:19:04.300
With a boost from Wingal Brave...

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:07.580
...Flogal attacks Enigman Ripple!

00:19:11.970 --> 00:19:13.460
I attack with Marron!

00:19:18.890 --> 00:19:20.210
My turn's finished.

00:19:20.210 --> 00:19:21.090
I draw.

00:19:22.090 --> 00:19:24.200
I ride Enigman Wave!

00:19:28.270 --> 00:19:29.820
Enigman Wave's skill!

00:19:30.360 --> 00:19:31.830
+1000 power!

00:19:34.010 --> 00:19:36.550
I call Masked Police, Grander!

00:19:38.700 --> 00:19:40.630
I attack Marron with Grander!

00:19:44.110 --> 00:19:46.000
I attack with Enigman Wave!

00:19:51.310 --> 00:19:52.470
That's the end of my turn.

00:19:53.810 --> 00:19:55.870
They each have 2 damage...

00:19:55.870 --> 00:19:57.540
EH2D!

00:19:57.540 --> 00:20:00.360
Looks like they've started by trading jabs...

00:20:00.770 --> 00:20:03.170
Barcgal, call Llew!

00:20:07.020 --> 00:20:08.320
Counterblast!

00:20:08.710 --> 00:20:12.700
I put Barcgal, Flogal and Llew into the Soul!

00:20:13.550 --> 00:20:16.280
Stand up, my avatar!

00:20:16.280 --> 00:20:17.840
I superior ride...

00:20:18.810 --> 00:20:20.790
...Blaster Blade!

00:20:32.480 --> 00:20:35.330
That Blaster Blade combo...

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:36.740
I haven't seen it in a long time.

00:20:36.740 --> 00:20:41.280
Yes, since Aichi was using that 
Shadow Paladin deck for awhile.

00:20:41.280 --> 00:20:43.790
It feels like Brother's come home!

00:20:53.230 --> 00:20:54.000
Call!

00:21:04.770 --> 00:21:05.600
Here it comes...

00:21:06.770 --> 00:21:09.590
Pongal's skill, Counterblast!

00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:12.640
I add Soul Saver Dragon to my hand!

00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:16.260
I'm ready.

00:21:16.640 --> 00:21:21.090
Mr. Mitsusada, I'm gonna charge 
at you with everything I've got!

00:21:27.800 --> 00:21:29.350
Just like I thought!

00:21:30.730 --> 00:21:35.270
As expected, Mitsusada 
sees right through Aichi.

00:21:35.270 --> 00:21:36.890
Naturally.

00:21:36.890 --> 00:21:41.260
That man ranks as one of the strongest 
Vanguard fighters in the world.

00:21:42.430 --> 00:21:47.060
Well, for someone who doesn't 
possess power like Ren, anyway...

00:21:49.590 --> 00:21:54.500
I haven't sensed him 
using Psyqualia so far...

00:21:55.190 --> 00:21:59.210
...but if he doesn't use it 
here, he won't beat Mitsusada.

00:22:01.350 --> 00:22:06.280
Did you want to show me 
your inevitable defeat?

00:22:07.810 --> 00:22:10.970
Well, Aichi?

00:23:51.490 --> 00:23:53.900
Misaki, that was really close.

00:23:53.900 --> 00:23:57.480
Yuri taught me to be mentally 
prepared for a fight.

00:23:57.480 --> 00:24:00.550
There's really nothin' better than being 
able to play against a strong fighter!

00:24:00.550 --> 00:24:03.720
Mr. Mitsusada sees through my tactics...

00:24:03.720 --> 00:24:06.740
I'd better leave the weak tricks behind 
and go after him for all I'm worth!

00:24:06.740 --> 00:24:09.130
Next time: The Man They Call "The Emperor"!

00:24:10.380 --> 00:24:14.220
Psyqualia's glow... The 
image is talking to me...

00:24:14.220 --> 00:24:17.390
Aichi, I'll answer your 
fighting spirit with my own!

00:24:17.390 --> 00:24:18.830
Mr. Mitsusada...
